Z||000004||MoneypitGT||02-19-2001||06:23 PM||||Well the QUAD project is officially started. I have mapped out the wiring harness and will probably finish the wiring this week, hopefully. I still haven't picked up Ben's engine crane yet, so that is a big hold up, but I do have an overall plan on how I am going to do things, just have to spend the money and get all the parts. I'll keep you posted. So did you decide what you are going to do yet?<BR>  Chris||||reg||14
Z||000005||Eric_PA||02-19-2001||07:19 PM||||Chris,<BR>I still havn't made up my mind on what is in the works for the Fiero. I recently fried the clutch out in my Sunfire when I decided to race a Ford Probe GTS. Put an OEM one back in and decided to trade it in on a Jeep Wrangler. Now I miss the darn thing since it was the fastest car I have ever owned so far. That will change when the GT gets done. I am thinking about a Stroker 2.8 to 3.1 with turbo and the Getrag 5 speed or possibly a 3.4 engine swap. Its amazing, I realized that you can't get 180 HP easily out of the 2.8's like I originally thought. Keep me posted on that conversion, I am really glad to see someone is making it happen.<BR>Eric||||reg||7
